// ============================================================================
// ZL Examples - Advanced - Shared<T>
//
// Managed objects are thread-confined by default. To let a worker thread touch
// one, wrap it: `new Shared<T>(value)` marks that value as shareable, and the
// thread closure captures the Shared wrapper rather than the object itself.
//
//   new Shared<T>(value)     wrap (the top-level share(value) does the same)
//   get() / setValue(v)      read / write - each one synchronised on its own
//   withLock(func(): T cb)   run cb under the cell's lock
//
// IMPORTANT: Shared<T> makes the capture LEGAL; it does not make it SAFE. Each
// cell operation is individually synchronised, but a read-modify-write across
// the get()/setValue() pair is not one operation: two threads can interleave
// their pairs and lose an update. Four threads doing 2000 unsynchronised
// increments of one cell land around 3000 of the expected 8000, which
// tests/zl/valid/concurrency_regressions/SharedLostUpdateMeasurement.zl
// measures on every run. For a real counter use the cell's own `withLock`
// (below), Atomic (Atomics.zl) or a lock (MutexLocks.zl).
// ============================================================================

class SharedState {
    func main(): void {
        var counter = new Shared<int>(0)
        log("initial " + counter.get())

        counter.setValue(10)
        log("after set " + counter.get())

        var worker = Thread.start(func() => counter.setValue(counter.get() + 5))
        Thread.join(worker)
        log("after worker " + counter.get())

        // The same increment under the cell's own lock: one indivisible
        // step, so it stays exact however many threads run it.
        counter.withLock(func(): int {
            var next = counter.get() + 1
            counter.setValue(next)
            return next
        })
        log("after withLock " + counter.get())

        var label = new Shared<string>("start")
        var renamer = Thread.start(func() => label.setValue("finished"))
        Thread.join(renamer)
        log("label " + label.get())
    }
}

// --- Expected output (verified by examples/run_all.sh) ---
// initial 0
// after set 10
// after worker 15
// after withLock 16
// label finished
// --- End expected output ---
